==Old English==

===Etymology 1===
{{PIE root|ang|h₁eḱ}}
From {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*ehwaz|t=horse}}, from {{inh|ang|ine-pro|*h₁éḱwos|t=horse}}. Cognate with {{cog|osx|ehuskalk|t=horse-rider}}, {{cog|goh|eha-}} (in personal names), {{cog|non|jór}}, {{cog|got|*𐌰𐌹𐍈𐍃}}. The Indo-European root is also the source of {{cog|la|equus}}, {{cog|ae||tr=aspa-}}, {{cog|sa|अश्व|tr=áśva}}, {{cog|xcl|էշ|t=donkey}}, Tocharian A ''[[yuk]]'' B ''[[yakwe]]'', {{cog|ine-bsl-pro|*ečwā-}} (Lithuanian ''[[ašva|ašvà]]''), Old Irish ''[[ech]]'' (Irish ''[[each]]'').

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|/eoh/|[eox]|lang=ang}}

